# Privacy Policy for Screamphone

**Effective Date:** November 24, 2026  
**Developer:** Iam_Mithra

Iam_Mithra ("we," "our," or "us") built the **Screamphone** mobile application as an ad-supported app with an optional in-app purchase to remove ads. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use the app.

## 1. Information We Collect
**Screamphone does not require user accounts and does not collect, store, or transmit your personal data to our servers.**

* **Device Sensors (Accelerometer / Motion Data):** The app accesses your device's motion sensors strictly in real time on your device to detect drops and shakes and trigger audio playback. Sensor data is never recorded, stored, or shared.
* **Local Preferences:** Your app settings (such as sensitivity levels, scream counter, and background mode status) are stored locally on your device.

## 2. Third-Party Services
While we do not collect personal information directly, Screamphone uses third-party services that may collect information used to identify your device:

* **Google AdMob (Advertising):** Displays banner ads in the free version of the app. AdMob may collect device identifiers (such as the Android Advertising ID), IP address, and usage data to serve personalized or non-personalized ads.
* **Google Play Billing:** Processes the optional "Go Ad-Free" in-app purchase. All payment and billing information is handled directly by Google Play; we do not have access to your financial details.

You can review Google's Privacy Policy here: [https://policies.google.com/privacy](https://policies.google.com/privacy)

## 3. Background Execution
If you choose to enable **Run in Background**, the app runs a local service to continue monitoring motion sensors while the app is minimized. You can disable this feature at any time inside the app.

## 4. Children's Privacy
Screamphone does not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13.

## 5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.

